  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support NRC Bangladesh Consortium under the Rohingya Response and National Resilience Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will contribute to addressing humanitarian needs gaps in the 2025 Rohingya Refugee Crisis Joint Response Plan (JRP), bridging the critical gaps in protection, education, health and SCCCM services. The project will implement a comprehensive set of activities through a coordinated and integrated approach. This will involve strengthening protection mechanisms, improving responses of the human rights situation through protection case management, access to information about rights and entitlements, and provision of legal assistance, as well as supporting housing, land, and property (HLP) rights. Additionally, the project will ensure access to essential services such as education, healthcare, and tailored assistance to persons with disabilities (PWDs) in the camps and host communities. Moreover, the project will regularly conduct protection monitoring in camps and host communities and produce a protection monitoring bulletin on a quarterly basis. The protection monitoring helps consortium members and contributes to protection sector in identifying key protection risks and trends through ongoing data collection to inform evidence-based advocacy and evidence-informed action for quality project outcomes.</narrative>
  </description>
